#: includes/modules/class-privacy.php:236
msgid "When the site owner connects the site, the plugin sends the site title, the site address, the site language, the email address of the site administrator, the plugin version and a random identifier of this installation to profotograaf.nl. Profotograaf uses the site title and administrator email address only to prefill the account sign-up form. The plugin sends no usage statistics or error reports."
msgstr ""

#: includes/modules/class-settings-page.php:302
msgid "Connecting shares this site's name and the administrator email address with Profotograaf, so it can fill them in for you if you create an account."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-settings-schema.php:102
msgid "Use Profotograaf photos in the editor"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-settings-schema.php:103
msgid "Lets editors who can upload files browse your Profotograaf photos in the block editor and add them to the Media Library. While this is on, the site asks Profotograaf for your photo list and downloads the photos an editor picks, and editors' browsers load thumbnails from profotograaf.nl. A photo an editor uses is stored on this site. Only galleries with embedding switched on are offered. While this is off, nothing is requested."
msgstr ""

#: includes/modules/class-privacy.php:233
msgid "Photo library in the editor"
msgstr ""

#: includes/modules/class-privacy.php:234
msgid "Only when the site owner turns on the media source: editors who can upload files can browse the photos of the connected Profotograaf account in the block editor. The site asks profotograaf.nl for the photo list and fetches the photos an editor picks. The editor's browser loads the thumbnails from profotograaf.nl, which receives that editor's IP address and browser details. A photo an editor uses is stored in the Media Library of this site and stays there until it is deleted. No visitor data is involved."
msgstr ""

